From a50876e8eaeb2940deb971c1afcdb32fb1ca4c98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SN Fast Sync <snfast@localhost.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:07:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(snjs): allow the push websocket on the sync server's own
 host (self-hosted server)

The app starts its websocket only for the first-party server (api.standardnotes.com), so a self-hosted server never got a push
channel even when a websocket URL was set for it. Now it is also started when the websocket URL points at the same host and port
as the sync server (for example https://sync.example.com:3123 and wss://sync.example.com:3123/ws). A third-party server with the
hosted websocket URL still gets none. Used for the planned PC-as-sync-server setup; changes nothing for the hosted server.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WeT9h5e494m7W6EHMFsEMq
